---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Colophon" description="How this site is built and tested, and its accessibility statement." current="colophon">
  <article class="measure-reading">
    <h1>Colophon</h1>
    <h2>How it is built</h2>
    <p>
      Static HTML generated with Astro from Markdown and YAML files. No runtime server, no database,
      no third-party scripts, fonts, or analytics. React is used for exactly one thing: the climb,
      the original 3D experience, which loads only when you ask for it.
    </p>
    <h2>How it is tested</h2>
    <p>
      Every change runs schema validation, a public and private boundary check, an em dash check, a
      provenance check, HTML validation, Playwright tests for structure, keyboard use, headers, and
      security, axe accessibility rules, and Lighthouse budgets.
    </p>
    <h2>Accessibility statement</h2>
    <p>
      The target is WCAG 2.2 AA on every page: a skip link, one heading per page, landmarks, visible
      focus, 44 pixel targets on primary actions, reduced motion honored, and no content that moves or
      plays on its own. If something does not work for you, email the address on the
      <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Version 1</h2>
    <p>
      The first version of this site is preserved unchanged at
      <a href="https://v1.khaylub.com" rel="noopener noreferrer">v1.khaylub.com</a> and as
      <a href="/climb/">the climb</a>. Its story is in <a href="/projects/khaylub-com-v1/">the case study</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
